			"Message": "feat(Mist): Implement WebSocket transport for Sky↔Cocoon direct path\n\nAdd a new WebSocket module to Mist implementing local-first JSON-RPC over WebSocket for the B7-S6 path. This removes the Tauri-invoke → Mountain-gRPC double hop on extension-API traffic (~95% of IPC volume in interactive sessions).\n\nNew dependencies: tokio-tungstenite, futures-util, serde, serde_json, hex, rand.\n\nImplementation includes:\n- `ServeLocal`: TCP listener on 127.0.0.1 accepting WebSocket connections\n- `Client`: Connection with background reader task for response dispatch\n- JSON-RPC wire format: text frames with `{id, method, params}` requests and `{id, result/error}` responses\n- Shared secret: 32-byte per-spawn secret for connection auth (X-Land-Secret header)\n- Backpressure: HashMap of pending requests by id with oneshot channels\n- Reconnect: Exponential backoff (100ms → 200ms → 400ms → 1s → 2s, capped at 5s), 30s dead channel report\n\nBinary frames are logged and ignored (reserved for phase 2 prost-encoded payloads). The X-Land-Secret header validation is TODO B7-S6 P1.1.\n\nThis enables the Sky↔Cocoon direct communication path while maintaining loopback-only security.",
			"SHA": "9998d8728702fc7b84998ee685cdcea0e5e109f1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T15:59:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				18,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Expand CHANGELOG with commit references and dates\n\nEnhance the CHANGELOG from a simple version list to a comprehensive\nnarrative of Mist's evolution. Each version now includes specific commit\nSHAs and dates for traceability, benefit-focused descriptions explaining\nwhat each feature provides (DNS isolation, security sandbox), and a clear\nreorganization: v2.1 (current workbench lift), v2.0 (DNS introduction),\nv1.x (placeholder phase), and v0.0 (inception).\n\nThis transforms the CHANGELOG from a mechanical change log into a story\nthat explains why each version matters to the project.",
			"SHA": "911e215ed09f9b43255eb50870af2e3235ec6d26"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T22:45:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				18,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Mist): Allow non-snake_case identifiers in module\n\nAdd `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` lint attribute to suppress Rust warnings for PascalCase naming conventions used throughout the CodeEditorLand project.\n\nThe project follows PascalCase for all identifiers (functions, variables, structs, modules) as documented in CLAUDE.md. This attribute permits the Mist module to use the same naming conventions as other Land components without generating lint warnings.",
			"SHA": "94e88d14f977906af3bfd02bcdc6c513bc78cf28"
		},
